    "result": "## Bug Fixed \u2713\n\nThe issue has been successfully fixed! Here's what was wrong and how I fixed it:\n\n**Root Cause:** When running `frai gate init --ci`, commander.js was parsing the `--ci` flag at the root `frai` command level (since `--ci` is defined as a root option), preventing it from being passed to the `frai-gate` subcommand.\n\n**Solution:** Modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to capture raw arguments directly from `process.argv` after the `gate` subcommand position, ensuring all flags (including `--ci`) are passed through to the spawned frai-gate process.\n\n**Verification:** \n- \u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` \u2192 Creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 Verified the direct `frai-gate init --ci` command still works correctly\n\nThe workflow file is now properly created when using the `frai` CLI wrapper!",
